---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Support — Hona Financial"
  description="Help with Hona: account access, draw requests, stakeholder access, billing and data."
>
  <section class="band-cream on-cream">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,1.5rem+2.2vw,3rem)">How can we help?</h1>

      <p style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        Write to <a href="mailto:support@honafinancial.com" style="border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;text-decoration:none">support@honafinancial.com</a>
        and a person — usually the person who built the app — will answer. Include
        the email address on your account and, if something went wrong, roughly
        when it happened.
      </p>

      <h2>I can't sign in</h2>
      <p>
        Open Hona, tap <strong>Forgot Password</strong> on the sign-in screen, and
        follow the link in the email. Reset links expire and can only be used
        once, so request a fresh one if the last is more than an hour old. Make
        sure you're using the same email address the account was created with —
        that's the most common cause.
      </p>

      <h2>I'm a lender and I was invited to a project</h2>
      <p>
        Download Hona from the App Store or Google Play, then create an account
        using <strong>the exact email address your contractor invited</strong>. The
        project appears in your Network automatically. Lender access is free —
        there is nothing to subscribe to.
      </p>

      <h2>A draw request isn't showing up</h2>
      <p>
        Draw status syncs live, but a phone with no signal will show the last
        state it could confirm. Pull to refresh, or close and reopen the project.
        If a request still isn't visible, check with the contractor that the
        project is shared with you and that draw status is switched on in your
        permissions — they control both.
      </p>

      <h2>I'm not receiving emails</h2>
      <p>
        Check junk and spam first; new sending domains are often filtered for a
        while. Hona sends from <strong>support@honafinancial.com</strong>, so
        marking one message as "not junk" usually fixes it permanently. If
        nothing has arrived at all, write to us and we'll look at the delivery log.
      </p>

      <h2>Billing and cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        Subscriptions are managed from Administration inside the app. Cancelling
        takes effect at the end of the current billing period, and you keep access
        until then. If you'd rather keep your records readable without an active
        subscription, View&nbsp;Only is $5 a month.
      </p>

      <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
      <p>
        Open <strong>Administration</strong> in the app and choose Cancel
        Subscription &amp; Delete Account. Details of what is removed and what is
        retained are on the <a href="/delete-account" style="border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;text-decoration:none">account deletion page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Something is wrong with the numbers</h2>
      <p>
        Tell us the project, the phase and what you expected to see. Hona keeps a
        full record of every receipt behind every figure, so a discrepancy is
        almost always traceable to a specific entry — and if it's a bug in our
        maths, we want to know today rather than after your next draw.
      </p>

      <hr class="rule" style="margin:3rem 0" />

      <p>
        <strong>Proprietary Solutions LLC DBA Hona Financial</strong><br />
        Queen Creek, Arizona<br />
        <a href="mailto:support@honafinancial.com" style="border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;text-decoration:none">support@honafinancial.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
